    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204561": {
      "title": "AVI Food Service Student Worker, Federal Work Study Only",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: AVI Food Service Student Worker, Federal Work Study Only McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: AVI Food Service Student Worker, Federal Work Study Only Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details AVI Food Service Student Worker, Federal Work Study Only Category: Student Worker Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Center for Experience and Oppo Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 8, 2026 Closes: Oct 13, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: PT No Benefits Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $15.00 - $15.00 Position ID: 204561 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Job Title: AVI Food Service Student Worker Effective Date: 02/17/2026 Reports to: AVI Managers Department: AVI Food Services Rate of Pay: Maryland Minimum Wage FSLA Status: Non-Exempt Location of Position: Roj Student Center, McDaniel College, 2 College Hill, Westminster, MD 21157 Duration of Appointment: August 5, 2026 to May 25, 2027 Schedule: Schedule is at discretion of supervisor Evaluation Procedures: Student workers are evaluated on a continuous basis. Scope: Support food service functions for AVI on McDaniel College property. Responsibilities: Assist in the preparation of hot and/or cold foods, and properly store foods, utilizing knowledge of temperature requirements and spoilage. Set up stations with entrées, soups, salads, breads, condiments, other food products and utensils. Interact with guests in the serving, retail, and dining areas. Follow proper guest service procedures whenever interacting with others by smiling, making eye contact, and greeting guests. Clean and sanitize workstations and equipment following all client and regulatory rules and procedures. Maintain a fast pace and ability to multitask when performing duties. Requirements: Current undergraduate student at McDaniel College Must have Federal Work Study as part of your Financial Aid package. Ability to work a flexible part-time schedule on campus. Previous food service experience preferred but not required. Strong work ethic Ability to communicate with other team members and other departments with professionalism and respect. Maintain a professional relationship with all team members, vendor representatives, supervisors, managers, customers, and client representatives. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
    },
    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204786": {
      "title": "Varsity Athletics Team Manager, Men's Basketball- Campus Employment & Federal Work Study",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Varsity Athletics Team Manager, Men's Basketball- Campus Employment & Federal Work Study McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Varsity Athletics Team Manager, Men's Basketball- Campus Employment & Federal Work Study Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Varsity Athletics Team Manager, Men's Basketball- Campus Employment & Federal Work Study Category: Student Worker Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Intercollegiate Athletics Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 14, 2026 Closes: Oct 26, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: PT No Benefits Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $15.00 - $15.00 Position ID: 204786 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Position: Varsity Athletics Team Manager, Men's Basketball Revision Dates: 09/2026 Reports to: Head Athletic Equipment Manager, Assistant Basketball Coach, and Head Basketball Coach Department: Athletics Rate of Pay: Maryland Minimum Wage FSLA Status: Non-exempt Location of Position: Gill Center, 2 College Hill, McDaniel College, Westminster, MD, 21157 Duration of Appointment: August 5, 2026 to May 25, 2027 Evaluation Procedures: Student workers are evaluated on a continuous basis. Scope: Provide support for assigned Varsity team during practices, games and events. Responsibilities: Attend practice and assist coaches with any items necessary Run the clock during practices Assist with equipment hand out Travel to away contests Keep scorebook during games Assist with Social Media accounts Schedule: 20 hours max a week, must have availability from 6-8AM or 4-8:30PM depending on schedule, must be available on weekends Must be able to attend away contests Must be available during January Term Requirements: Qualifications: Current student at McDaniel College Highly organized and detail oriented Knowledge of the rules of assigned sport Discretion and reliability in sensitive and confidential matters are vital Physical Characteristics: This position requires some physical activity.  This position does have some lifting involved but not more than 30 pounds at a time. The overall setting of the job is in the gymnasium. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected charac